 "stimulus_html": "Suppose you’re rolling the same colored 6-sided die 10 times. Let <span data-math=\"O\">O</span>, <span data-math=\"G\">G</span>, and <span data-math=\"B\">B</span> represent the number of times the die lands with an orange, green, and blue side up, respectively. Find these probabilities (round to 4 decimal places):",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 516913,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"P(O \\leq 7)\">P(O \\leq 7)</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The 6-sided die has 3 orange faces, 2 green faces, and 1 blue face.</p>\n<p>There are 3 orange faces out of 6 sides, so p is <span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{6} = \\frac{1}{2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{P}}\\left( {{\\text{O }} \\leq {\\text{ }}7} \\right)\"></span> in 10 tries.</p>\n<p>Google Sheets can be used to compute cumulative binomial distributions. The event is sides less than or equal to 5.</p>\n<p>In Google Sheets, enter “=BINOMDIST(7, 10, 0.5, TRUE)” to get your answer: 0.9453.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0.9453"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 516914,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"P(G = 5)\">P(G = 5)</span>\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The 6-sided die has 3 orange faces, 2 green faces, and 1 blue face.</p>\n<p>Binomial formula: For a binomial experiment with n trials and p probability of success in each trial, then P(number of a successes) = <span data-math=\"nCa \\times {p^a} \\times {\\left( {1 - p} \\right)^{n - a}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>There are 2 green faces out of 6 sides, so p is <span data-math=\"\\frac{2}{6} = \\frac{1}{3}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>P(exactly 5 greens in10 rolls) =<span data-math=\"\\left( {10C5} \\right){\\left( {\\frac{1}{3}} \\right)^5}{\\left( {1 - \\frac{1}{3}} \\right)^{10 - 5}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left( {252} \\right){\\left( {\\frac{1}{3}} \\right)^5}{\\left( {\\frac{2}{3}} \\right)^5} \\approx 0.1366\"></span></p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0.1366"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 516915,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"P(1 \\leq B \\leq 4)\">P(1 \\leq B \\leq 4)</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"1{\\text{ }} \\leq {\\text{ B }} \\leq {\\text{ }}4\"></span></p>\n<p>You are looking for the outcome {1, 2, 3, 4}.</p>\n<p>To do this, you will find <span data-math=\"{\\text{B }} \\leq {\\text{ }}4\"></span> and subtract <span data-math=\"{\\text{B }} \\leq {\\text{ }}0\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The 6-sided die has 3 orange faces, 2 green faces, and 1 blue face.</p>\n<p>The probability of a blue side is 1/6.</p>\n<p>In Google Sheets, enter “=BINOMDIST(4,10, 0.1666666, TRUE)” to get the answer 0.98454.</p>\n<p>In Google Sheets, enter “=BINOMDIST(0,10, 0.1666666, TRUE)” to get the answer 0.16151.</p>\n<p>Subtracting the two, you get 0.8230.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0.8230"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
